[4/7] No runtime YAML config hot-reload
  Status: PASS
  Evidence: Classes ConfigWatcher, ReloadableConfig, ConfigChangeListener, OperatorConfigSnapshot were removed during hot-reload removal. grep for these names returned no matches. jackson-dataformat-yaml dependency removed from operator/framework/pom.xml (still present transitively via fabric8). Plan was updated to reflect removal.

[5/7] No leader election / metrics port / watched namespace hot-reload
  Status: PASS
  Evidence: grep for reload patterns targeting leaderElection, metricsPort, watchedNamespace returned no matches. Leader election, metrics port, and watched namespace are configured at startup via env/values and remain fixed.

[6/7] No webhook metrics/tracing/generic test framework
  Status: PASS
  Evidence: Source code under operator/framework/src/main/java contains no webhook-specific metrics, tracing, OpenTelemetry, Micrometer, Prometheus, or Jaeger integrations. MetricsServer is for the operator's own /metrics endpoint, not webhooks. Documentation mentions metrics only in the context of the existing MetricsHealthServer.

[7/7] Webhook server not shared with metrics/health port
  Status: PASS
  Evidence: WebhookServer defaults to port 8443. MetricsHealthServer uses port 8080. Deployment exposes both ports separately; Service exposes metrics on 8080 and webhook on 443/8443. README states "Admission webhooks run on a separate TLS server."

