NOTES / MINOR OBSERVATIONS
================================================================================

1. Java package for v1alpha2 CRD classes is `com.example.echooperator.api.v2` instead of `com.example.echooperator.api.v1alpha2`. The API version string is correctly `example.com/v1alpha2` and the CRD generator emits `v1alpha2`. This is a naming convention deviation, not a functional gap.

2. Plan requested a separate `templates/webhook-service.yaml`; implementation added the webhook port to the existing `templates/service.yaml`. The rendered Helm output still exposes port 443 -> targetPort webhook and is functionally equivalent.

3. Plan references a class `ConversionWebhookHandlerTest`; actual test class is `ConversionHandlerTest`. The SDK interface `ConversionWebhookHandler` exists and is tested.

4. Default Helm values do not render ValidatingWebhookConfiguration/MutatingWebhookConfiguration because the operator self-registers them at runtime. Setting `webhook.createWebhookConfigurations=true` renders them correctly.

